cff-version: 1.2.0
message: 'To cite package "responses.build" in publications use:'
type: software
license: BSD-2-Clause
title: 'responses.build: A Workflow for Harmonising Physiological Response-Curve Data
  into a Documented Standard Structure'
version: 0.1.0.9000
doi: 10.1016/j.ecoinf.2024.102773
abstract: The `responses.build` package provides a workflow to harmonise physiological
  response-curve data - leaf gas exchange, hydraulic vulnerability, and fluorescence
  response curves - from diverse sources into a documented, relational structure. It
  is a fork of `traits.build` (Wenk et al, 2024, <https://doi.org/10.1016/j.ecoinf.2024.102773>,
  <https://github.com/traitecoevo/traits.build>), which harmonises single-valued trait
  data; this package extends the same data model to measurements that form curves. It
  was built to support AusFizz (<https://github.com/traitecoevo/ausfizz>). For the shared
  data model and workflow concepts see <https://traitecoevo.github.io/traits.build-book/>.
